.SH NAME
QChildEvent \- Event parameters for child object events
.SH SYNOPSIS
.br
.PP
\fC#include <qevent.h>\fR
.PP
Inherits QEvent.
.PP
.SS "Public Members"
.in +1c
.ti -1c
.BI "\fBQChildEvent\fR ( Type " "type" ", QObject * child )"
.br
.ti -1c
.BI "QObject* \fBchild\fR () const"
.br
.ti -1c
.BI "bool \fBinserted\fR () const"
.br
.ti -1c
.BI "bool \fBremoved\fR () const"
.br
.in -1c
.SH DESCRIPTION
The QChildEvent class contains event parameters for child object events.
.PP
Child events are sent to objects when children are inserted or removed.
.PP
The handler for these events is QObject::childEvent().
.SH MEMBER FUNCTION DOCUMENTATION
.SH "QChildEvent::QChildEvent ( Type type, QObject * child )"
Constructs a child event object.
.PP
The \fItype\fR parameter must be either \fIQEvent::ChildInserted\fR or \fIQEvent::ChildRemoved.\fR
.SH "QObject * QChildEvent::child () const"
Returns the child widget inserted or removed.
.SH "bool QChildEvent::inserted () const"
Returns TRUE if the widget received a new child.
.SH "bool QChildEvent::removed () const"
Returns TRUE if the object lost a child.
